ing to go to  the No Deal scenario and then just  finally I'm a little late on the show  we'll be hearing from Nick Bowles who's  pushing for this idea of a kind of  Norway plus staying in a single market I  mean is that something that you think  labour could support well obviously we'd  have to hear what Nick says about it  he's put in a number of different ways  this idea of a Norway I mean I went to  Norway to study the Norway model as it's  called for for  all days and I didn't think it would  really work very well for the United  Kingdom it obviously works well for  Norway and when it was put as a  proposition to Parliament we didn't get  a majority and the Prime Minister says  she's not interested in it so  considerate then or is it something that  you you just don't think well at the  moment we need to see quite how it's put  but at the moment I'm not sure that it's  something that's very attractive but I  think what you're seeing now is that as  we run into this vote people are saying  well what other options are there I  think the person who needs to answer  that question is the Prime Minister okay  you could argue as well that she's been  slightly hamstrung by put a divider  Parliament as well so well she had the  snap election and lost her majority so I  mean it's it's not you know just  Parliament I get to the Prime Minister  actually she's the author Oh misfortune  okay okay that's Donna thank you very  much thank you
 

